     "content": "### The Verdict: **Accept (Strong Yes)**\n\nFrom a purely compensation standpoint, **this is an exceptional outcome.** \n\nA **$200,000 sign-on bonus** at Google L6 is at the absolute top end of what their compensation committee approves, typically reserved strictly for buying out unvested FAANG equity. By matching your base at **$240k** and adding that sign-on, Google effectively conceded to your demands without forcing you into an extended standoff.\n\n---\n\n### The Updated Math: What You Will Actually Make\n\nHere is what your realized earnings look like under Google's standard **33% / 33% / 22% / 12%** front-loaded vesting schedule (assuming the sign-on is paid upfront in Year 1):\n\n| Component | Current Meta | Google Year 1 | Google Year 2 | Google Year 3 | Google Year 4 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Salary** | $240,000 | $240,000 | $240,000 | $240,000 | $240,000 |\n| **Target Bonus** | $36,000 *(15%)* | $48,000 *(20%)* | $48,000 | $48,000 | $48,000 |\n| **Initial RSU Vest** | ~$250,000 | $356,400 *(33%)* | $356,400 *(33%)* | $237,600 *(22%)* | $129,600 *(12%)* |\n| **Sign-On Bonus** | $0 | **$200,000** | $0 | $0 | $0 |\n| **Refresher Stack** *(est.)* | \u2014 | \u2014 | +~$25,000 | +~$60,000 | +~$100,000 |\n| **Total Realized TC** | **~$526,000** | **~$844,400** | **~$669,400** | **~$585,600** | **~$517,600** |\n\n#### Why this is a win:\n- **Year 1:** You are making **~$844,400**, an immediate **+$318,000 (+60%) cash and equity surge** over Meta.\n- **4-Year Baseline:** Before any stock appreciation or annual refreshers, you are guaranteed **$2.43M** over 4 years (~$608,000/yr average).\n- **With Modest Refreshers:** Your 4-year total comp will land around **$2.6M\u2013$2.7M** (~$650,000/yr average), easily outpacing Meta\u2019s current baseline by roughly **$500,000+** over the cycle.\n\n---\n\n### 2 Crucial Details to Verify Before Signing\n\nBefore you put pen to paper, ask the recruiter to confirm two specific